{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777141249,"nonce":"RwLuc1pWvX4nrGBlBI/tKVcvxa4=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAgWr8A","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/91","origin":"github"},"title":"BizzyBoat: switch nav source to FCU EKF3-fused topics (CG-referenced)","message":"## Summary\n\nSwitch BizzyBoat's primary nav source from raw GPS + IMU (current path through `mru_transform`) to ArduPilot's EKF3-fused MAVROS topics. EKF3 already produces a CG-referenced solution using the calibrated `GPS_POS*` / `INS_POS*` lever arms; today's pipeline silently absorbs those lever arms instead. This proposal is a near drop-in topic swap, no new dependencies.\n\n## Current state\n\n`mru_transform` consumes three raw FCU topics (per `bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml:24-26`):\n\n| Role | Topic | Reference point |\n|---|---|---|\n| Orientation | `mavros/imu/data` | base_link (FCU EKF3 attitude) |\n| Position | `mavros/global_position/raw/fix` | **Forward GPS antenna phase center** |\n| Velocity | `mavros/global_position/raw/gps_vel` | **Forward GPS antenna** |\n\n`mru_transform` is a priority-voting passthrough, not a Kalman blender. It stamps everything as `bizzy/odom` / `bizzy/base_link`, but the reported XY position is actually the **forward antenna phase center**, not base_link/CG. With `GPS_POS1 = (+0.835, 0, +0.89 ENU)` that's a heading-dependent ~0.84 m bias forward of CG (plus 0.89 m up if anyone consumes Z). RTK-fix noise is cm-class, so this lever arm dominates the absolute position error.\n\n## Proposal\n\nHave `mru_transform` (or its successor) source nav from EKF3-fused topics, all of which are reported at the body origin EKF3 was calibrated to — which on BizzyBoat is the CG, per `docs/bizzyboat_gps_config_2026-04-02.md` and the configured offsets in `bizzyboat_project11/config/fcu/bizzyboat_fcu_custom.param`:\n\n```\nGPS_POS1_X/Y/Z = ( 0.835, 0, -0.89)   # forward antenna, NED\nGPS_POS2_X/Y/Z = (-0.835, 0, -0.89)   # aft antenna\nINS_POS1/2/3   = (-0.99,  0, -0.05)   # IMU 0.99 m aft of CG\nAHRS_ORIENTATION = 0\nEK3_SRC1_POSXY/VELXY = 3   # GPS\nEK3_SRC1_YAW         = 2   # GPS dual-antenna heading\nCOMPASS_ENABLE       = 0   # mag disabled\n```\n\nTopic swap (config-only, in `bizzyboat.yaml`):\n\n| Role | Today | Proposed | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Position | `mavros/global_position/raw/fix` | `mavros/global_position/global` | Same `NavSatFix` type; WGS84; EKF3-fused at CG |\n| Orientation | `mavros/imu/data` | `mavros/local_position/pose` | `PoseStamped`; needs an mru_transform input adapter (small) |\n| Velocity (body) | `mavros/global_position/raw/gps_vel` | `mavros/local_position/velocity_body` | `TwistStamped`; surge/sway/yaw-rate at CG, body FLU |\n\nNet effect: same TF tree, same `/bizzy/odom` contract for Nav2, but position/velocity/attitude all live at base_link/CG with the lever arms compensated by EKF3.\n\n## Reference-frame analysis (why this works)\n\nArduPilot's EKF3 runs at the IMU and lever-arm-corrects every measurement back to the **body origin** (the common (0,0,0) all `*_POS_*` offsets are measured from). The body origin is whatever the user calibrates it to be. BizzyBoat has both `GPS_POS*` and `INS_POS*` non-zero and consistent, with the GPS doc explicitly stating \"BizzyBoat origin is at the CG.\" So:\n\n- `local_position/pose`, `local_position/velocity_local`, `local_position/velocity_body`, `global_position/global`, `global_position/local` → all reported at **CG / base_link**.\n- `global_position/raw/*` → **forward antenna** (GPS1).\n- `imu/data` orientation → base_link; accel/gyro in `imu/data` → IMU location.\n\nSwitching to EKF3-fused topics means we stop double-handling the lever arm.\n\n## Open questions / decisions before implementation\n\n1. **`local_position` origin**: `local_position/*` is in a local ENU frame whose origin is the EKF home, set at first 3D fix (since BizzyBoat intentionally never calls `set_gps_global_origin` per the autonomy stack convention — `mavros.guided_target` warnings are expected noise). `local_position/pose.position` will therefore drift by power-cycle. **Mitigation**: ignore `local_position/pose.position` and only use its `orientation`; take position from `global_position/global` (WGS84, no origin issue). Velocity from `local_position/velocity_body` is body-frame, so origin-independent. Confirm this is acceptable before coding.\n2. **Topic rates**: verify `local_position/*` and `global_position/global` publish at rates compatible with Nav2 / collision_monitor expectations. ArduPilot's `SR*_POSITION` stream rates may need tuning.\n3. **mru_transform input adapter**: today's nav inputs are `Imu` + `NavSatFix` + `TwistStamped`. The proposed inputs are `PoseStamped` + `NavSatFix` + `TwistStamped`. mru_transform's input type hierarchy may need a small extension to accept `PoseStamped` for orientation (or we keep `imu/data` for orientation since it's already EKF3 attitude — only orientation changes nothing, no rotation lever arm).\n4. **Failure modes**: when EKF3 is unhealthy (e.g., GPS dropout), `local_position/*` continues to publish dead-reckoned state with growing covariance. Do we want a fallback to raw GPS? Today's priority-voting handles this implicitly; with fused inputs we may want to gate on `mavros/state` or EKF status.\n5. **IzzyBoat parity**: IzzyBoat (`izzyboat_project11/config/izzyboat.yaml:19-21`) uses the same three raw topics and has its own configured `GPS_POS*` / `INS_POS*`. Proposal could land BizzyBoat-only first, then mirror to IzzyBoat once validated. Or land both together. **Decision needed.**\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- SBG Ellipse-D as a ROS-side nav source — SBG is hydro payload, not core nav (per `project_bizzyboat_sonar_architecture.md`).\n- Replacing `mru_transform` with `robot_localization` — explicit non-goal: we want to *use* the FCU's EKF, not run a parallel one.\n- Setting a global origin to make `local_position/pose.position` repeatable — conflicts with the \"ArduPilot is dumb actuator\" autonomy convention.\n\n## References\n\n- BizzyBoat GPS / antenna config: `docs/bizzyboat_gps_config_2026-04-02.md`\n- BizzyBoat FCU custom params: `bizzyboat_project11/config/fcu/bizzyboat_fcu_custom.param`\n- Current nav wiring: `bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml:24-26`, `:42-44`\n- Reference geometry: `bizzyboat_project11/docs/bizzyboat_reference_geometry.md`\n- Related: #87 (mavros plugin allowlist) — the EKF3 plugins (`local_position`) are already in APM defaults, but #87 should keep them in the allowlist.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}